// storage-latency.kql — storage utilisation and IO pressure, for SSD v1 vs v2 comparison
//
// Input:    AzureMetrics
// Consumed by: azure-native/workbooks/, benchmark-integration/
//
// IMPORTANT — this query is supplementary during benchmarks, not authoritative.
// Premium SSD v2 is in preview, and platform telemetry for v2-backed servers may be
// incomplete. A flat or missing series here means "no data from the platform", which is
// visually identical to "no IO happened". The authoritative storage signal during a
// benchmark is the Innodb_data_* counters the Layer 2 collector writes to ADX; see
// grafana/dashboards/benchmark-ssd-v1-vs-v2.json.
//
// Flexible Server exposes io_consumption_percent — the fraction of the provisioned IOPS
// budget in use — but no read/write latency metric. Latency has to be inferred from the
// engine side, which is another reason Layer 2 leads here.

let lookback = 24h;
let bucket = 5m;
AzureMetrics
| where TimeGenerated > ago(lookback)
| where MetricName in (
    'io_consumption_percent',
    'storage_percent',
    'storage_used',
    'storage_limit',
    'data_storage_used',
    'binlog_storage_used',
    'Innodb_data_writes',
    'Innodb_buffer_pool_reads',
    'Innodb_buffer_pool_read_requests'
  )
| summarize Avg = avg(Average), Max = max(Maximum) by bin(TimeGenerated, bucket), MetricName, Resource
| order by TimeGenerated asc

// --- Buffer pool hit ratio from platform metrics ---------------------------------------
// Sustained dips mean the working set has outgrown the buffer pool, which turns logical
// reads into physical ones and makes the storage tier suddenly matter a great deal.
//
// AzureMetrics
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
// | where MetricName in ('Innodb_buffer_pool_reads', 'Innodb_buffer_pool_read_requests')
// | summarize Value = sum(Total) by bin(TimeGenerated, 5m), MetricName
// | evaluate pivot(MetricName, sum(Value))
// | where Innodb_buffer_pool_read_requests > 0
// | extend HitRatio = 1.0 - (Innodb_buffer_pool_reads * 1.0 / Innodb_buffer_pool_read_requests)
// | project TimeGenerated, HitRatio
// | order by TimeGenerated asc

// --- Storage headroom ------------------------------------------------------------------
// Flexible Server storage cannot be shrunk, and autogrow has a ceiling. Trend this rather
// than alerting only on a threshold, so the runway is known before it is short.
//
// AzureMetrics
// | where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
// | where MetricName == 'storage_percent'
// | summarize MaxPercent = max(Maximum) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), Resource
// | order by TimeGenerated asc
